From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: camera_sensor: Add S5KJN1 sensor properties

The Samsung S5KJN1 applies both exposure and analogue gain two frames
after the frame they are written in. Without static properties libcamera
assumes a gain delay of one, so the software ISP's AGC credits each
frame's statistics to the wrong gain and hunts: on a Zinwa Q25 the rear
camera's brightness swung between about 17 and 125 (of 255) every four
frames and never settled.

Measured on a Zinwa Q25 by streaming the CAMSV video node directly
(4080x3072, 70 ms frames) and stepping V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN (1x<->8x,
8x<->32x) and V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE (2000<->8000 lines) on the sensor
subdevice: a write as frame N arrived showed in frame N+2 in all 21
steps, and in N+3 in all 14 written 40 ms later instead. The vertical
blanking delay is taken to follow the exposure's, as for the other
SMIA-style sensors; it was not measured.

The pixel is 0.64 um, and the test pattern values are the driver's menu
order, those of the SMIA test pattern register.
---
 src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
index 20cfd0b..e4fecc8 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -571,6 +571,22 @@ const CameraSensorProperties *CameraSensorProperties::get(const std::string &sen
 			},
 			.sensorDelays = { },
 		} },
+		{ "s5kjn1", {
+			.unitCellSize = { 640, 640 },
+			.testPatternModes = {
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeOff, 0 },
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeSolidColor, 1 },
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeColorBars, 2 },
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeColorBarsFadeToGray, 3 },
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModePn9, 4 },
+			},
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
+		} },
 		{ "vd55g1", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 2160, 2160 },
 			.testPatternModes = {
